# Blend modes on paper, 256x64. Six cells left to right; each is a gold 36x36 square with a blue circle of radius 13
# centered 10px right of the square's center, so the circle covers the square's right half and spills past its right
# edge. The circle carries a blend: key. Cell 1: no blend, a plain blue circle. Cell 2: multiply, the circle is a dark
# olive green, darker than both gold and blue. Cell 3: screen, the circle is pale pink, lighter than both. Cell 4:
# overlay, the circle is a muted tan-gold, distinct from plain blue. Cell 5: add, the circle is plain white. Cell 6:
# erase, the circle cuts a round hole through the square and shows paper through it.
@target shapes/blends.png 256x64

layer cells
  rect 36x36 at:21,32 fill:p.gold
  circle 13 at:31,32 fill:p.blue
  rect 36x36 at:63,32 fill:p.gold
  circle 13 at:73,32 fill:p.blue blend:multiply
  rect 36x36 at:105,32 fill:p.gold
  circle 13 at:115,32 fill:p.blue blend:screen
  rect 36x36 at:147,32 fill:p.gold
  circle 13 at:157,32 fill:p.blue blend:overlay
  rect 36x36 at:189,32 fill:p.gold
  circle 13 at:199,32 fill:p.blue blend:add
  rect 36x36 at:231,32 fill:p.gold
  circle 13 at:241,32 fill:p.blue blend:erase
